	(text "PWR_FLAG: these rails reach their loads only through passive parts (the edge fingers, USB-C, the P-FET, the SS34s, the bucks' inductors)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 35.56 226.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d7a28bdb-f1d4-5add-ae4a-5982e7330887")
	)
	(text "Power tree: +5V is the OR of three sources.\n  CONS_5V  edge 26, the console's VR1 (a 78M05, 0.5 A, on the original CA018087 board, which also feeds the\n           console's RAM and controllers), through Q3 AO3401A (D = CONS_5V, S = +5V): on unless its gate CONS_OFF is\n           high; with the gate high only its body diode is left, which never passes anything back into the console.\n  VBUS     USB-C, through D4 SS34.\n  PRE5V    edge 11, the adapter's raw DC (9-13 V; universal boards only, ahead of the power switch, so live whenever\n           the adapter is plugged in): JP2 bridged jumper (cut it to take nothing from pin 11), F1 0.35 A PTC, R30 2.2R\n           inrush limit, U10 AP63205 5 V buck, D8 SS34.  Never ground pin 11: on a universal console it is the adapter.\nCONS_OFF = VBUS OR PRE5V (D9 BAT54C, R23 100k): either one turns the console path off, so with raw DC present the\ncart takes nothing from VR1.  R3 / R22 4.7k hold the SS34s' reverse leakage (0.5 mA at 25 C, 20 mA at 100 C) off\nthe OR's inputs, so the console path stays on (tools/audit/spice_checks.py).  +5V feeds the 74HCT541 / '08 / '14,\nthe PHI2 buffer, the WS2812, the AP2112K LDO -> +3V3_RP (every RP2354B supply pin: it rises with +5V, so the\n5V-tolerant pads are never unpowered with 5 V on them) and the AP63203 buck -> +3V3 (ESP32-S3, microSD, CP2102N).\nTP17, TP18, TP16, TP2, TP1, TP11 and the rp-core DVDD pad are bring-up test points."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 35.56 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "39279557-e5f1-5214-b8f1-67f19356e1a6")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
